.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.TH sqop-validate-userid 1 "February 2025" "sqop 0.38.0" 
.SH "نام (NAME)"
sqop\-validate\-userid \- Validate a User ID in an OpenPGP Certificate
.SH "خلاصه دستور (SYNOPSIS)"
\fBsqop validate\-userid\fR [\fB\-\-addr\-spec\-only\fR] [\fB\-\-debug\fR] [\fB\-\-validate\-at\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] <\fIUSERID\fR> <\fICERTS\fR> 
.SH "توضیحات (DESCRIPTION)"
Validate a User ID in an OpenPGP Certificate
.SH "گزینه‌ها (OPTIONS)"
.TP
\fB\-\-addr\-spec\-only\fR
Treat USERID as an e\-mail address, and matched only against the e\-mail address part of each correctly bound User ID
.TP
\fB\-\-debug\fR
Emit verbose output for debugging
.TP
\fB\-\-validate\-at\fR \fI<VALIDATE_AT>\fR
Evaluate the validity of the User ID at the specified time, not at the current time
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help
.TP
<\fIUSERID\fR>
The User ID to validate
.TP
<\fICERTS\fR>
Authority OpenPGP certificates, i.e. trust roots
